# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Sheet -> CSV data source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app reads one student profile per sheet row at runtime.
#
# 1. Make the sheet readable: Share -> General access -> "Anyone with the link"
#    -> Viewer. (No "Publish to web" step is required for the URL below.)
# 2. Grab the sheet id from its URL:
#      https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<SHEET_ID>/edit
# 3. Build the CSV endpoint and paste it below:
#      https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<SHEET_ID>/gviz/tq?tqx=out:csv
# 4. Copy this file to ".env.local" (git-ignored) with your real value, then
#    restart `npm run dev` (Vite only reads env files at startup).
#
# Column headers are matched in src/lib/loadProfiles.ts (COLUMN_MAP) — update
# that map if your sheet's header text differs. Google Drive photo links
# (drive.google.com/open?id=...) are converted to viewable images automatically;
# the uploaded files must be shared "anyone with the link can view".
#
# When this is empty/unset, the app falls back to the sample profile in
# src/data/profiles.ts so it still runs during development.
#
# TIP: to preview the full flow (multi-student dropdown + CSV parsing) WITHOUT a
# Google Sheet, point it at the bundled sample file that Vite serves from public/:
#   VITE_SHEET_CSV_URL=/students.sample.csv
VITE_SHEET_CSV_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<SHEET_ID>/gviz/tq?tqx=out:csv
